<title>INDIA: India approves law to set up port tariff regulator.</title>
<headline>India approves law to set up port tariff regulator.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian cabinet on Friday approved the promulgation of an ordinance to enable the appointment of an independent tariff regulation authority to fix and revise port charges, the Press Trust of India (PTI) said. India allowed private firms to set up port facilities under an economic reform programme launched in 1991.</p>
<p>The new law is expected to enable a transparent functioning of privatised port facilities.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom, +91-11-301 2024</p>
</text>
